Good news — **you don't need to run migrations.** Your cloud Supabase project is already fully on the new schema. I checked the live DB (`mndzexcqfubygquimkmn`):

| Thing | Status |
|---|---|
| All 17 tables + `schedules` + `webhook_hooks` | ✔ present |
| All enums incl. `hook_status` | ✔ |
| RLS policies on every table | ✔ |
| Storage bucket `chat-attachments` | ✔ |
| Realtime publication (chat, run_activities, approvals, notifications, schedules, webhook_hooks) | ✔ |
| Limit/system triggers on threads + groups | ✔ |
| `handle_new_user()` function | ✔ |

**One gap found:** the `on_auth_user_created` **trigger on `auth.users` is missing** (function exists, trigger doesn't). Without it, future Google sign-ups get no Personal workspace, no profile, no membership, no PERSONAL/SITE/WORKFLOWS/INVITES groups — so P5 chat will break for new users.

Fix: paste this into Supabase Dashboard → SQL Editor for `mndzexcqfubygquimkmn` → Run:

```sql
DROP TRIGGER IF EXISTS on_auth_user_created ON auth.users;
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION "public"."handle_new_user"()
RETURNS trigger
LANGUAGE plpgsql
SECURITY DEFINER
SET search_path = public
AS $$
DECLARE
  ws_id text;
  grp_personal text;
  grp_site text;
  grp_workflows text;
  grp_invites text;
  prf_id text;
  wme_id text;
BEGIN
  ws_id := 'wp_' || replace(gen_random_uuid()::text, '-', '');
  INSERT INTO "public"."workspaces" ("id", "name", "created_by", "is_default")
  VALUES (ws_id, 'Personal', NEW.id, true);

  wme_id := 'wme_' || replace(gen_random_uuid()::text, '-', '');
  INSERT INTO "public"."workspace_members" ("id", "workspace_id", "user_id", "role")
  VALUES (wme_id, ws_id, NEW.id, 'owner');

  prf_id := 'prf_' || replace(gen_random_uuid()::text, '-', '');
  INSERT INTO "public"."user_profiles" ("id", "user_id")
  VALUES (prf_id, NEW.id);

  grp_personal := 'grp_' || replace(gen_random_uuid()::text, '-', '');
  INSERT INTO "public"."groups" ("id", "workspace_id", "user_id", "name", "kind", "position")
  VALUES (grp_personal, ws_id, NEW.id, 'PERSONAL', 'system', 0);

  grp_site := 'grp_' || replace(gen_random_uuid()::text, '-', '');
  INSERT INTO "public"."groups" ("id", "workspace_id", "user_id", "name", "kind", "position")
  VALUES (grp_site, ws_id, NEW.id, 'SITE', 'system', 1);

  grp_workflows := 'grp_' || replace(gen_random_uuid()::text, '-', '');
  INSERT INTO "public"."groups" ("id", "workspace_id", "user_id", "name", "kind", "position")
  VALUES (grp_workflows, ws_id, NEW.id, 'WORKFLOWS', 'system', 2);

  grp_invites := 'grp_' || replace(gen_random_uuid()::text, '-', '');
  INSERT INTO "public"."groups" ("id", "workspace_id", "user_id", "name", "kind", "position")
  VALUES (grp_invites, ws_id, NEW.id, 'INVITES', 'system', 3);

  RETURN NEW;
END;
$$;

CREATE TRIGGER on_auth_user_created
  AFTER INSERT ON auth.users
  FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION "public"."handle_new_user"();
```

That's the only DB action before P5. If you have an existing test account, its workspace is already fine — the trigger only affects brand-new signups.

